// stopped it. `failed`: another system failed it.
type FleetActivityResultReads string

// FollowedSetup THE VERSION THE DEVICE FOLLOWS, handed at every check-in: "every device follows exactly
// one". The device sets what it holds, and sets it again when it drifts if `mode` is
// `enforce`. Its protection rules and its monitors are handed; its settings are a later slice.
type FollowedSetup struct {
	// ApplyAgain "ENFORCE RE-APPLIES WHENEVER A DEVICE DRIFTS." `true` when `mode` is `enforce` and the
	// device last said it drifted from this very version (`setup_state.state` `drifted`): set
	// it again, whole. `false` otherwise — under `recommend`, which "applies once" and turns
	// the drift into a failing rule instead, and for a device that holds the version or has
	// not applied it yet.
	ApplyAgain bool `json:"apply_again"`

	// Mode "ENFORCE OR RECOMMEND." `enforce` — "Enforce re-applies whenever a device drifts".
	// `recommend` — "Recommend applies once and reports drift as a failing rule". Held per kind
	// and per device a version is applied to, and handed to the device with the version.
	Mode SetupMode `json:"mode"`

	// Monitors WHAT THE DEVICE IS TO MEASURE (ONPLO-3225): the version's monitors, each read once a
	// minute, battery health and a certificate's days at each check-in, and sent every five
	// minutes by `reportMonitorReadings`. Empty for a version that watches nothing. A device nothing
	// is applied to watches what its kind's setup ships with, as it ships (ONPLO-4972).
	Monitors SetupMonitors `json:"monitors"`

	// ProtectionRules "THE RULES THAT DECIDE HEALTH." Nine, and always all nine: "Each rule is on or off, Required
	// or Recommended, and a rule that measures something carries its own value, which the setup
	// may change inside its range."
	//
	// A RULE IS NEVER ASKED OF A KIND IT CANNOT APPLY TO, whatever a setup says: "a rule that
	// cannot apply to a kind of device is never asked of it". WHICH KINDS EACH CAN APPLY TO is
	// written on each rule below, word for word from the Protection rules block (decision 0800
	// point 1). A one-job thing is in none: it runs no agent. "A rule switched on for a kind it
	// cannot apply to is shown greyed with the reason, and judges no device of that kind" — so it
	// is never refused here, and a rule that is on judges only the devices it can be read from.
	//
	// SWITCHING A RULE OFF IS LOUD: "switching one off announces itself on every device that
	// follows it."
	ProtectionRules ProtectionRules `json:"protection_rules"`

	// SetupId The setup it follows. `null` only for a device nothing is applied to in an account
	// environment whose setups that ship are not made yet; they are made the first time
	// somebody reads the setups, and the rules handed are theirs as they ship.
	SetupId *Id `json:"setup_id"`

	// VersionNumber The version it follows. A device nothing is applied to follows version 1 of the setup that ships for its kind.
	VersionNumber int `json:"version_number"`
}

// FreshnessWindowHours "Managed-and-compliant freshness window": "how recent a device's last reading must be for the
// managed-and-compliant condition to count it", in whole hours, 24 unless changed. "Set in hours, from
// 1 hour to 7 days, on every plan" (decision 0978): no part of it needs Devices' Premium seat.
