// ShippedSetup WHICH OF THE SETUPS THAT SHIP: "Four setups ship and are on from the first device: Computer
// · Phone or tablet · Server · One-job thing. A business account environment gets a fifth,
// Your own device at work." Each can be renamed and edited, and none can be deleted: "The
// shipped setups cannot be deleted, only edited."
//
// YOUR OWN DEVICE AT WORK fits a computer and a phone or tablet, and requires six rules (decision
// 0800 point 2): "disk encryption · screen lock · passcode · supported OS · find-my · not
// jailbroken; firewall, malware protection and backup recommended".
type ShippedSetup string

// SoftwareConnectionAlert WHAT AN APP FROM A CONNECTED STORE RAISES WHEN ITS CONNECTION ENDS OR BREAKS, as Integrations
// says it in its events (`ConnectionEnded`, `ConnectionStoppedWorking`) and the spec lane ruled on
// 21 October 2026 (ONPLO-2652). "Nothing that depends on a connection is left to discover the
// breakage on its own next run: each dependent raises the alert in its own app, pointing back at
// this row." The row it points back at is the connection `source.connection_id` names.
//
// `connection_removed`: the connection is gone for good. The item STAYS, reading "⚠ connection
// removed — pick a new one"; a removed connection never deletes an item. It installs nothing new
// until it is moved onto a connection with `moveSoftwareItemToConnectedStore`, so it is not made
// Required meanwhile (`store_connection_removed`). What its devices already installed stays
// installed: uninstalling is a person's choice when they take the item off, never the system's.
//
// `connection_stopped_working`: the connection turned NOT WORKING, and `cause` is Integrations'
// own sentence for why, shown as it is and never branched on. It stays until a later stop
// replaces it, the connection is removed, or the item is moved — onto that same connection too,
// which is how a person says they have seen it.
//
// A DISCONNECTED CONNECTION RAISES NOTHING HERE. The item keeps naming it, and its state is read
// from Integrations when the row is shown: "A consumer copies no status."
//
// NOT DECLARED YET, because neither exists for any item: the licence count a connected store
// keeps, which reads none while the connection is removed, and the Failed list, where an install
// that fails while the connection is not working gives "the store connection stopped working".
type SoftwareConnectionAlert struct {
	// Cause Integrations' plain cause, for `connection_stopped_working` alone: a sentence for a person,
	// from an open list, so a program decides nothing from its wording. `null` for a removal.
	Cause *string `json:"cause"`

	// Kind Which alert.
	Kind SoftwareConnectionAlertKind `json:"kind"`

	// Since When it happened, as Integrations says it: when the connection was removed
	// (`ended_at`), or when it stopped working (`stopped_at`).
	Since Timestamp `json:"since"`
}

// SoftwareConnectionAlertKind Which alert.
type SoftwareConnectionAlertKind string

// SoftwareFailureReason "The reason the platform gave — not enough space, the store refused the licence, the
// detection rule did not match, the person declined" (Software). `other` is any reason the
// page does not name. A CLOSED LIST, so the Failed list can say each in a person's words and
// group by it.
type SoftwareFailureReason string

