// Sourcing HOW THE BOX WAS COME BY. `hosted` is a rented server you patch. A field, never a boundary.
type Sourcing string

// StagedWaves A CHANGE OFFERED TO A SHARE OF THE DEVICES FIRST: an update, on an update schedule; a
// version, on a setup; a Required software item's change (`SoftwareRollout`, ONPLO-4322). ONE
// RULE FOR EVERY PAGE: a setup's staged rollout "follows the same
// rule as an update schedule's staged waves", with the same ranges and defaults. Which devices
// are in the first wave is "picked by Onplo across the schedule's groups", and on a setup
// across what the version is applied to.
//
// THE PICK, ON A SCHEDULE: the schedule, the update and the device draw one number of a hundred,
// and the device is in the first wave when it is under `first_wave_percent`. So the same device
// stays in the same wave for one update on one schedule, whoever joins or leaves it, and each
// update draws its own. It is a share device by device, so a schedule of few devices may have
// nobody in its first wave, and then every device waits the days before the rest. OR THE TEST
// GROUP, when the schedule sends it first (`UpdateSchedule.test_group_first`).
//
// THE AUTOMATIC PAUSE. "On Premium the rest are paused when too many of the first wave fail",
// at `pause_threshold_percent`. A setup's rollout reads on the setup (`Setup.paused_rollouts`), and
// a schedule's update on the schedule (`UpdateSchedule.paused_updates`), and a software item's
// change on the item (`SoftwareRollout.paused`).
//
// ON A SCHEDULE, THE FIRST WAVE IS EVERY DEVICE OF IT THAT REPORTED THE UPDATE, including one that
// has since installed it, and failing is reading `update_failing` now. So clearing a failing update
// lowers the share. A device that installed an update before this was kept is not counted.
type StagedWaves struct {
	// FirstWavePercent The share of the devices offered it first, as a whole percentage. 10 unless you say.
	FirstWavePercent int `json:"first_wave_percent"`

	// PauseThresholdPercent "Premium. The rest are paused when this share of the first wave's devices fails": a whole
	// percentage, at this share or over. `null` never pauses. Left out of a request it is `null`,
	// because waves are sent whole; the 20% the page starts from is the page's to fill in for
	// somebody holding the seat.
	//
	// SETTING IT NEEDS DEVICES' PREMIUM SEAT, asked of Account (`not_in_plan`, or
	// `account_unavailable` when Account cannot be asked). The seat is needed to set the number,
	// not to keep it (decision 0824 rule 2): one that stands stays when the seat lapses, sending
	// it again asks nothing, and `null` never needs a seat.
	//
	// LIFTING THE PAUSE IS A CHANGE TO WHAT HOLDS THIS NUMBER: raise it, or take it away. A save
	// that leaves it alone lifts nothing, so the rest do not move on to what failed while a fix
	// is being prepared.
	PauseThresholdPercent *int `json:"pause_threshold_percent,omitempty"`

	// RestAfterDays Whole days after the first wave is offered it before every other device is. 3 unless
	// you say.
	RestAfterDays int `json:"rest_after_days"`
}

