// ReportInstalledSoftwareWithBody A device reports the software installed on it, one part at a time
//
// THE INSTALLED SOFTWARE LIST (ONPLO-4946): "one entry per app, with its name, its publisher
// and its version". A device calls it about itself, as it calls `checkIn` (decision 0644, rule
// 4), and no permission is evaluated.
//
// IN PARTS, APART FROM THE CHECK-IN: "A list has hundreds of entries, so it may arrive in
// parts, apart from the check-in." A request body holds at most 100 KiB, measured at every
// character's longest escaped form, so a part holds at most fifteen entries, and a list at most
// a hundred parts. A list of one part is sent as part 1 of 1.
//
// "A NEW LIST REPLACES THE LAST ONE ONLY ONCE IT HAS ARRIVED WHOLE, AND UNTIL THEN THE LAST
// WHOLE LIST STANDS." A list is whole when every part from 1 to `part_count` has arrived. Then
// it replaces the device's last whole list, and one audit event says so, with how many apps
// each held. A part of a new list, while another is still arriving, drops the one arriving: the
// device started over. A part sent twice replaces itself, so a part whose answer was lost is
// sent again. A part of the list that is already whole changes nothing.
//
// WHAT IS COLLECTED IS SETTINGS → COLLECTION & PRIVACY'S: the full list on a company-owned
// device and on a shared one, the work profile only on a person's own. Which entries the device
// sends is the device's to read; Devices keeps what arrives.
//
// PAST LISTS ARE KEPT (ONPLO-4951): "past lists are inventory snapshots". A whole list replaces the last
// one as the device's list, and the last one is kept for Settings → Collection & privacy → "Inventory
