// the state it reads: `device_is_enrolled` or `device_is_assigned`, which is also what closing
// it twice answers. One in repair, in lost mode or retired is refused `device_is_in_repair`,
// `device_is_lost` or `device_is_retired`. Nothing is changed.
//
// WHEN THE TASK SERVICE COULD NOT BE ASKED, the answer is 503 `tasks_unavailable`. The reclaim
// stays open, and the same request can be sent again. WHEN IDENTITY DID NOT SAY WHICH KIND OF
// ACCOUNT ENVIRONMENT THIS IS, the answer is 503 `authorization_unavailable`: the answer names a
// state, and not known is not personal.
