// RecycleDeviceWithBody Record that a retired device was recycled
//
// THE DISPOSAL OF A RETIRED DEVICE, RECORDED: "RECYCLED records the disposal", and "RECYCLE
// starts from RETIRED only, and nothing leaves RECYCLED" (Business environment → Devices app →
// Lifecycle; decision 0761, point 1). The device reads `recycled` from then on, and keeps its
// retirement receipt beside the recycle receipt.
//
// NOTHING IS SENT TO THE DEVICE, AND NOTHING IS WIPED OR RETIRED HERE. A retired device's
// management profile is gone, or its receipt says it may still be on it, and its certificates
// are ended. Recycling is a fact about where the hardware went, written on its record. (Until
// ONPLO-1510 the Company devices page said "Recycle wipes the device, retires it, and renders
// a receipt"; the spec lane changed it to the Lifecycle page's reading on 18 October 2026.)
//
// THE RECYCLE RECEIPT is what the spec lane ruled on ONPLO-1510: who recorded the disposal and
// when, who took the device (a recycler or a buyer, required), their certificate or reference
// number, and a note. Devices keeps it as this record, as it keeps the retirement receipt; the
// file rendered into Storage for the auditor waits on Storage holding a folder for Devices.
//
// FROM `retired` ONLY. A device in any other state is refused, and the code names the state it
// is in: `device_is_enrolled`, `device_is_assigned`, `device_is_in_repair` or `device_is_lost`.
// A device already recycled is refused `device_is_recycled`, and its receipt is not
// rewritten. The other states of `LifecycleState` cannot be reached yet, so no refusal names
// them yet. Nothing is changed by a refusal. WHEN IDENTITY DID NOT SAY WHICH KIND OF ACCOUNT
// ENVIRONMENT THIS IS, the call answers 503 `authorization_unavailable` and nothing is
// changed: whether a device that is not retired reads `enrolled` or `assigned` is the kind's
// to say, and not known is not personal. Ask again.
//
// A RECYCLED DEVICE IS REFUSED EVERY OTHER MOVE AS A RETIRED ONE IS, `device_is_retired`: it
// was retired, and nothing leaves RECYCLED.
//
// ONE DEVICE, ITS OWN PERMISSION, ASKED OF THIS DEVICE. Holding it on the device, or on a
// group the device is in, is enough. ONE AUDIT RECORD naming who recorded it.
//
// Takes any type of body and a specified content type.
//
// Corresponds with POST /devices/{device_id}/recycling (the `RecycleDevice` operationId).
