// ONPLO-2678). While "Second person on wipe and retire" is on, and it is on by default, a
// company's own or shared record in a business account environment waits for a second person,
// who reads the reason: "a second person is needed on every company device, the asker's own
// included". Such a record is refused here `second_person_needed`, and nothing is written: it is
// asked with `askToRetireRecordMadeByHand`, and retires when a second person approves
// (ONPLO-2908). With the switch off it retires here. A record of a person's own device, and
// every record in a personal account environment, waits for nobody, as an un-enrol does: it
// reaches nothing and deletes nothing. A record whose retirement is already asked and waiting
// is refused `retirement_waiting`: it retires by that ask's answer, or once the asker takes it
// back. WHEN IDENTITY DID NOT SAY WHICH KIND OF ACCOUNT ENVIRONMENT THIS IS, the call answers
// 503 `authorization_unavailable` and nothing is written: not known is not personal. Ask again.
