// CreateRequiredSoftwareItemWithBody Add software that installs by itself
//
// A REQUIRED ITEM "installs at the next check-in" on every device it is applied to, so adding one
// is pushing software and asks for `devices:software-item.deploy` beside adding it (decision 0721
// rule 1). Its own operation, so the push permission is asked every time and never for only some
// bodies, and in ONE CALL, so no moment exists in which the item stands as available and somebody
// installs it.
//
// A FLOW OR AN AGENT NEVER GETS HERE. An install a flow or an agent starts waits for a person
// (decision 0763 rule 1). Pushing software is ring 2 and never an agent's, so an agent is refused,
// and so is a machine's key while its build door is closed (`ring_requires_person`). The ask a
// flow's install lands as waits on the script approval, which this file does not declare yet.
//
// It is applied to nothing yet: applying it is `applyRequiredSoftwareItemToGroups` and
// `applyRequiredSoftwareItemToDevices`.
//
// NOT AN APP FROM A CONNECTED STORE. One would ask a third permission, pointing the item at a
// connection, and an operation asks at most one beside its own (decision 0657). So it is added
// available to install with `createConnectedStoreSoftwareItem`, applied to nothing, and then
// made Required with `makeSoftwareItemRequired`. One sent here is refused with 409
// `connected_store_item_has_its_own_operation`.
//
// Takes any type of body and a specified content type.
//
// Corresponds with POST /required-software-items (the `CreateRequiredSoftwareItem` operationId).
