	// MoveSoftwareItemToConnectedStoreWithBodyWithResponse Move a software item onto an app from a connected store
	//
	// "EDIT AN ITEM — its source", when the new source is an app from Apple Apps and Books or Managed
	// Google Play. The item keeps its id, its name, what it is applied to and what happens on
	// removal; its source is the one sent, and `version_policy`, when sent, replaces its own.
	//
	// IT TAKES TWO PERMISSIONS, THE PAIR ADDING ONE TAKES: changing the item, and pointing it at a
	// connection, `integrations:connection.assign`. Your credential must carry both. They are asked
	// as one question, and a refusal is one 403 whose detail names both (decision 0657).
	//
	// NOT A REQUIRED ITEM. Its devices would install the new app by themselves, which is pushing
	// software and asks a third permission (decision 0721 rule 1), and an operation asks at most one
	// beside its own. Take it off Required with `updateSoftwareItem`, move it here, and make it
	// Required again with `makeSoftwareItemRequired` (`software_item_is_required`). A BLOCKED ITEM
	// moved here becomes available to install: it names no software any more.
	//
	// THE CONNECTION IS JUDGED AS ADDING ONE JUDGES IT: the company's, to that store. Anything else
	// is 422 at `/body/source/connection_id` (`store_connection_not_usable`).
	//
	// THE CONNECTION THEN SAYS SO, in the same act. A package the item installed before is let go as
	// removing the item lets it go (decision 0833 rule 3), and a connection it pointed at before
	// has the item's use taken back. Sending the connection and app it already has changes nothing
	// and is answered as it is — unless the item raises a `connection_alert`.
	//
	// A MOVE CLEARS THE ITEM'S `connection_alert`. Moved onto the connection that stopped working,
	// the alert is cleared and nothing else changes: that is how a person says they have seen it.
	// One whose connection was removed is judged again like any other, so the removed connection
	// itself is 422 at `/body/source/connection_id`.
