	// UpdateSoftwareItemStagedRolloutWithBodyWithResponse Change how a software item's changes are rolled out
	//
	// "STAGED ROLLOUT — Roll a change to a percentage of devices first" (ONPLO-4434, the spec lane's
	// ruling of 7 November 2026): the item's Staged rollout, First wave, Days before the rest and
	// Pause threshold, with the setup's ranges and defaults (`StagedWaves`), and whether the Test
	// group goes first (`test_group_first`). Only what is sent changes.
	//
	// WHAT IS STAGED: a Required item's version changing (`changeRequiredSoftwareItemInstallation`
	// naming another package version or store app, or another version policy: "a new pin, a raised
	// minimum" — ONPLO-4456), and widening a Required item's Applied to
	// (`applyRequiredSoftwareItemToGroups`, `applyRequiredSoftwareItemToDevices`), over the devices
	// the change reaches. Available to install and Blocked items are never staged: nothing installs
	// by itself, so there is nothing to stage. A NEW RELEASE UNDER KEEP LATEST IS NOT STAGED (the
	// spec lane's ruling of 8 November 2026, ONPLO-4475): the device takes it as its store offers
	// it. To stage a release, pin the version and move the pin. Kept whatever the mode is, so the page shows it under
	// Required alone and an item made Required again keeps the choice.
	//
	// A CHANGE HERE DECIDES THE NEXT ROLLOUT and moves no device that waits in one: the waves are
	// picked once, when the change is made. ONE EXCEPTION, THE PAUSE: raising the threshold or taking
	// it away lifts a rollout it paused, as on a setup. So this installs nothing by itself and asks
	// no push permission.
	//
	// SETTING A PAUSE THRESHOLD NEEDS DEVICES' PREMIUM SEAT, asked of Account (`StagedWaves`).
	//
	// Takes any type of body and a specified content type, and returns a wrapper object for the known response body format(s).
