// ListFleetActivityWithResponse What happened across the fleet, with who did it
//
// "EVERYTHING THAT HAPPENED TO EVERY DEVICE: who did what, from where, and what the device
// answered" (Business environment → Devices app → Activity). One entry per event in Devices,
// newest first, read from the one audit log: Devices keeps no second log, and the same entries
// appear in Account → Activity, filtered to Devices.
//
// READING IT IS ITS OWN PERMISSION, and opening it is itself written to the log. The catalogue
// gives it in a business account environment alone, across the whole environment. Your own trail
// is never gated, and is Account's `listMyActivity`.
//
// NARROWED BY DEVICE, KIND OF EVENT, WHO AND WHEN, as the page filters, each combined with the
// others. A device is matched as the event's target: an act on a group, such as a device moved
// into one, names the group, and is found by its kind and not by the device. A kind is the
// page's word for the acts behind it, and only kinds whose acts exist are declared (ONPLO-3055).
//
// WHO IS ALWAYS NAMED, AND A LINE SAYS WHAT BECAME OF THE ACT (ONPLO-3020). When the names cannot be
// read no line is shown: the page answers 503 `names_unavailable`, which is sent again, or the
// usual 403 when identity refuses to say who is a guest here.
