// ListBuiltInReportsWithResponse The reports that come with Devices
//
// THE BUILT-IN REPORTS, IN THE ORDER THE PAGE NAMES THEM, and the same for everybody who may read
// reports. Each is "a saved filter plus columns over the register", written here and stored
// nowhere: `opens` says what to ask `listDevices` and which columns to show. So each "shows and
// counts only the devices its reader may see", as the register does.
//
// A BUILT-IN REPORT "CAN BE NEITHER CHANGED NOR DELETED". It has a `key` and no id, and no
// operation takes a key.
//
// TWO ARE A COMPANY'S: Unassigned devices and the Your-own-device boundary. A personal account
// environment "has neither an assignee list nor a company boundary, so the page says that in one
// line rather than showing an empty report": there the report has `opens: null`, and
// `not_here_because` is the line.
//
// THE YOUR-OWN-DEVICE BOUNDARY IS "WHAT THE COMPANY SEES, PER DEVICE": the devices a person owns,
// and in `opens.boundary` what the company sees on each. That is what a check-in carries today and
// Settings → Collection & privacy fixes on, so it is the same for every such device. It grows with
// the check-in, and it comes to differ by device when the page's collection switches arrive.
//
