// UpdateCollectionAndPrivacyWithBodyWithResponse Change what is collected and how long it is kept
//
// "HEALTH READINGS KEPT": how long past readings are kept "for the auditor who samples a period", 0
// to 400 whole days. "At 0 only the latest reading is held": a device's latest reading is never deleted,
// because its health word is read from it.
//
// "MONITOR MEASUREMENTS KEPT" (ONPLO-4971): how long the numbers behind a monitor are kept, 0 to 400
// whole days. "What is kept for this window is one number an hour per measurement, the worst of that
// hour; the readings a minute apart are kept two days, to judge a monitor's Holds for." At 0 no hour
// is kept, and the minutes still stay their two days.
//
// "INVENTORY SNAPSHOTS KEPT" (ONPLO-4951): how long a device's past installed software lists are kept,
// "so “what changed on this laptop” is answerable", 0 to 400 whole days. A list a newer whole one
// replaced is a snapshot, kept from the moment it was replaced. "At 0 only the latest reading is held":
// the device's own whole list is never deleted.
//
// "WHAT MONITORS MEASURE" (ONPLO-4971): "Switching this off silences the monitors." Off, a device is
// handed no monitor at its next check-in, so it measures nothing; a reading it still sends is not kept
// and is counted not watched (`reportMonitorReadings`); and a finding standing on it clears, as one
// whose thing is no longer watched does. Switched on again, each device is handed its setup's monitors
// at its next check-in. Nothing already kept is deleted by the switch: the window does that.
//
// A SHORTER WINDOW TAKES EFFECT AT THE READINGS SWEEP'S NEXT PASS. Nothing is deleted by the change
// itself.
//
// "EVERY CHANGE HERE RE-VERSIONS THE PRIVACY NOTICE shown at enrolment and tells the people it
// affects" (ONPLO-2573). Each ownership kind's notice takes its next version, and each person holding
// a device of that kind in use hears `devices.privacy-notice-changed`, once per kind. Whoever made the
// change is not told. A change that changes nothing makes no version.
//
// "0 TO 90 FREE · UP TO 400 PREMIUM" (ONPLO-2572, after decision 0824 rule 2), for each window. Raising a
// window above 90, and above where it stands, needs Devices' Premium seat, held by the one acting: refused without it
// (`not_in_plan`). A window already past 90 STANDS when that seat lapses, and lowering one never needs a
// seat, so neither does sending the number it already holds. Whether the seat is held is Account's to
// answer, and is asked only for a number above 90. WHEN ACCOUNT CANNOT BE ASKED, the answer is 503
// `account_unavailable`, never `not_in_plan` in its place: nothing changed, and the same request can be
// sent again. (Until ONPLO-2572 a number above 90 was refused at the field: "Devices cannot read an
// account environment's plan".)
//
// A CHANGE TO WHAT IT ALREADY HOLDS WRITES NOTHING, and is answered as it stands.
//
// Takes any type of body and a specified content type, and returns a wrapper object for the known response body format(s).
//
// Corresponds with PATCH /collection-and-privacy (the `UpdateCollectionAndPrivacy` operationId).
func (c *ClientWithResponses) UpdateCollectionAndPrivacyWithBodyWithResponse(ctx context.Context, contentType string, body io.Reader, reqEditors ...RequestEditorFn) (*UpdateCollectionAndPrivacyResponse, error) {
	rsp, err := c.UpdateCollectionAndPrivacyWithBody(ctx, contentType, body, reqEditors...)
	if err != nil {
		return nil, err
	}
	return ParseUpdateCollectionAndPrivacyResponse(rsp)
}

