// UpdateDeviceDefaultsWithBodyWithResponse Change the device defaults
//
// ONLY WHAT IS SENT CHANGES.
//
// MARK ONE GROUP AS THE TEST GROUP: "the only thing that makes it the Test group is that it is marked
// as such — one per account environment, static or smart like any other." Marking a group takes the
// job from the group that had it, so the mark is this page's and not the group's, and `null` marks
// none. The group must be one you may see; one you may not see, one that does not exist and one being
// deleted are each refused `404`, alike. A group that is deleted takes the mark with it.
//
// SET THE LEAD TIME, in whole days from 1 to 30: how many days early the Test group receives a
// setup's change, or an update on a schedule whose waves send it first, "set once in Settings →
// Device defaults, never per rollout".
//
// SET THE FRESHNESS WINDOW, in whole hours from 1 to 168: how recent a device's last reading must be
// for the managed-and-compliant condition to count it. It is read each time the condition is asked,
// so a change decides the next answer (`getManagedAndCompliantCondition`).
//
// A ROLLOUT ALREADY STARTED KEEPS ITS WAVES. The Test group and its lead time are read when a version is applied
// (`Setup.test_group_first`), so a change decides the next rollout and moves no device that waits.
// AN UPDATE SCHEDULE READS BOTH WHEN IT IS READ (`UpdateSchedule.test_group_first`): it stores no
// wave, so a change moves when its devices are offered an update from then on.
//
// A CHANGE TO WHAT IT ALREADY HOLDS WRITES NOTHING, and is answered as it stands.
//
// Takes any type of body and a specified content type, and returns a wrapper object for the known response body format(s).
//
