// SilenceDeviceMonitorWithBodyWithResponse Silence a monitor on one device for a maintenance period
//
// "A PERSON MAY SILENCE ONE FOR A MAINTENANCE PERIOD WITH A REASON. A silence covers one monitor
// on one device, or on one group, and it needs both the reason and the end of the period" (the
// Setups page). This is the one device; `silenceGroupMonitor` is the group. The answer is the
// silence as kept.
//
// WHAT IS SILENCED IS WHAT IS WATCHED: a measurement, and for a service or a scheduled job the
// name the device knows it by (`monitored_name`, sent for those two and for no other). A silence
// names what is watched rather than a version of a setup, so it holds through a new version, or a
// new setup, while the period lasts. A measurement the device's setup does not watch is kept all
// the same, and holds once it does.
//
// "A SILENCE HOLDS A MONITOR'S FINDING AND ITS ALERT FOR A MAINTENANCE PERIOD ... AND THE DEVICE
// KEEPS MEASURING" (Settings → Action safeguards). It ENDS BY ITSELF at `ends_at`; nothing here
// ends one sooner. No device measures yet (this file's header), so a silence holds nothing until
// one does.
//
// THE END IS A MOMENT AFTER NOW, AND NO LATER THAN THE LONGEST SILENCE: Settings → Action
// safeguards → "the longest silence", 7 days unless changed there (`getActionSafeguards`'s
// `longest_monitor_silence_days`), counted from now. An end that is past is refused
// `silence_ends_in_the_past`, one too far `silence_longer_than_allowed`, both at `/body/ends_at`.
// Two silences of the same thing may stand together; the later end is the one that counts.
//
// A RETIRED DEVICE IS REFUSED `device_is_retired`: it measures nothing again.
//
// ITS OWN PERMISSION, `devices:monitor.suspend`, "its own right, because a safeguard nobody can be
// granted is not a safeguard", granted across the account environment alone. The device is asked
// of identity too (`devices:device.read`), and one you may not see answers as one that does not
// exist. ONE AUDIT RECORD, with the reason and the end of the period: "Silencing one is its own
// permission, logged with the reason and the end of the maintenance period."
//
// Takes any type of body and a specified content type, and returns a wrapper object for the known response body format(s).
//
// Corresponds with POST /device-monitor-silences (the `SilenceDeviceMonitor` operationId).
func (c *ClientWithResponses) SilenceDeviceMonitorWithBodyWithResponse(ctx context.Context, contentType string, body io.Reader, reqEditors ...RequestEditorFn) (*SilenceDeviceMonitorResponse, error) {
	rsp, err := c.SilenceDeviceMonitorWithBody(ctx, contentType, body, reqEditors...)
	if err != nil {
		return nil, err
	}
	return ParseSilenceDeviceMonitorResponse(rsp)
}

