// GetDevicesEventPreferencesWithResponse Which of Devices' own events notify you
//
// EVERY CATEGORY DEVICES POSTS UNDER, each with your three switches — in the app, by email,
// by push — and what the company set for it: `none`, `default` (a starting point you may
// change) or `required`. Yours alone, in the account environment this credential acts in.
//
// THE TWELVE CATEGORIES, one per event the Notification preferences page lists. A name is
// permanent, like every id:
//
//	devices.required-rule-failing      a device failing a required rule
//	devices.device-not-heard-from      a device not heard from
//	devices.monitor-over-threshold     a monitor over its threshold
//	devices.update-past-deadline       an update past its deadline
//	devices.install-failed             a setup or software install that failed on a device
//	devices.approval-waiting           a wipe or a script waiting for your approval
//	devices.remote-session-on-yours    a remote session on a device you own
//	devices.warranty-or-lease-ending   a warranty or lease ending
//	devices.exemption-running-out      an exemption about to run out
//	devices.bulk-action-finished       a bulk action you started finished
//	devices.action-dropped             an action you asked for that was dropped
//	devices.privacy-notice-changed     the privacy notice of a device you hold changed
//
// A BULK ACTION YOU STARTED FINISHED is the one notification a job sends when it ends, with
// how many devices are done, waiting and failed, and only to the person who started it. Only
// a company's devices have bulk actions, so it is listed everywhere and sent only there.
//
// AN ACTION YOU ASKED FOR THAT WAS DROPPED is sent when a device stayed offline past its
// queued action expiry, so the restart, lock or message never reached it, and only to the
// person who asked. An action of a bulk job is told with its job, never on its own.
//
// THE PRIVACY NOTICE OF A DEVICE YOU HOLD CHANGED is sent when Collection & privacy changes
// (`updateCollectionAndPrivacy`) or the company's own words on a notice do (`changePrivacyNotice`),
// to each person holding a device of that ownership kind in use,
// and never to whoever made the change. It names the ownership kind and the version.
//
// NOT GATED. "Devices's own events, below, is always editable here": which of them reach you
// is nothing a company gives or takes away. What a company may set is whether you are told
// at all, and that is `company_rule`.
//
// ACCOUNT'S GENERAL CHANNELS STILL DECIDE. An event with `email` on sends no email while
// email is off in Account's Notification preferences; the choice here is kept.
//
// ONLY A PERSON HAS EVENT CHOICES. An agent or a machine is refused with 403
// `ring_requires_person`.
//
// A CATEGORY YOU NEVER CHOSE answers where Devices starts it: in the app for all twelve, and by
// push as well for `devices.approval-waiting` and `devices.remote-session-on-yours`.
//
// THE NOTIFICATIONS SERVICE HOLDS THE CHOICES (decision 0760), and Devices asks it. WHEN
// THE NOTIFICATIONS SERVICE CANNOT BE ASKED the answer is 503 `notifications_unavailable`,
// never the choices from a copy and never where each category starts: ask again.
//
// Returns a wrapper object for the known response body format(s).
//
// Corresponds with GET /devices-event-preferences (the `GetDevicesEventPreferences` operationId).
func (c *ClientWithResponses) GetDevicesEventPreferencesWithResponse(ctx context.Context, reqEditors ...RequestEditorFn) (*GetDevicesEventPreferencesResponse, error) {
	rsp, err := c.GetDevicesEventPreferences(ctx, reqEditors...)
	if err != nil {
		return nil, err
	}
	return ParseGetDevicesEventPreferencesResponse(rsp)
}

