// ListDevicesFeaturesWithResponse Your own Devices features
//
// DEVICES' DEFAULT, FREE AND PREMIUM FEATURES, each with its group, whether you hold it and
// whether it is shown. "Three groups: (1) Default — always on", "(2) Free — included; switch
// on/off freely", "(3) Premium — premium features, unlocked by a Premium subscription for
// this app".
//
// A PREMIUM FEATURE YOU DO NOT HOLD IS LISTED, with `held: false`: it is "shown locked with
// an upgrade path when you don't hold one".
//
// NOT IN THIS LIST: a capability the whole account environment shares, whose one switch is
// the company's and asks a permission; and a trial.
//
// YOURS ALONE, per account environment, because what you hold differs between them. NOT
// GATED: a switch here changes what you see and no access.
//
// `feature_id` IS THE FEATURE'S PERMANENT ID in Devices' feature list, `device-register`
// for the register itself.
//
// A FEATURE IS LISTED ONLY WHERE IT EXISTS: one only a company has, such as zero-touch
// enrolment, is not in a person's own account environment's list.
//
// WHEN ACCOUNT CANNOT BE ASKED who holds Devices' Premium seat, the answer is 503
// `account_unavailable`, never a list with `held: false` in its place: not known is not "not
// held". The same request can be sent again.
//
// Returns a wrapper object for the known response body format(s).
//
// Corresponds with GET /devices-features (the `ListDevicesFeatures` operationId).
