//
// THE PERSON NAMED ACCEPTS THE HAND-OVER FORM, and the device reads `assigned`, held by them. "The
// acceptance records that version", the one the hand-over was rendered from. Accepted on the
// device, or "in the person's own Devices app" for a thing with no screen of Onplo's.
//
// NOT GATED: ONLY THE PERSON NAMED. Whether the caller is that person is the hand-over's to say,
// so no company gives or takes away accepting what was handed to you. Anybody else, like a
// device with no hand-over waiting, is answered 404 and is never told whose it is.
