//
// ONLY AN INSTALL THAT FAILED FOR THE VERSION THE ITEM INSTALLS NOW. Anything else is refused
// `install_not_failed`, and nothing is recorded: an install that worked, one still waiting,
// an item this device was never handed, and one that failed for an older version. That last
// one is waiting already: the next check-in hands the version the item installs now.
//
// IT HANDS ONLY WHAT A CHECK-IN WOULD HAND. An item that is no longer Required, or no longer
// reaches the device, is not handed when the install goes back to waiting, and waits until
// it does.
//
// A RETIRED DEVICE IS REFUSED `device_is_retired`: its management profile is gone, and it
// checks in no more (ONPLO-2666). A device or an item that is not there answers 404, the
// same for one in another environment.
//
// ITS OWN PERMISSION, ASKED OF THIS DEVICE. Holding it on the device, or on a group the device
// is in, is enough. "On all of them", a selection at once, is
// `trySoftwareInstallAgainOnDevices` (ONPLO-3665). (Until ONPLO-3665 this said it was not
// declared yet.)
//
// ONE AUDIT RECORD naming who asked, a change to the device that names the item.
//
// Returns a wrapper object for the known response body format(s).
//
// Corresponds with POST /devices/{device_id}/software-installs/{software_item_id}/another-try (the `TrySoftwareInstallAgain` operationId).
