// StartEnrolmentThroughLinkWithBodyWithResponse Start enrolling your device through an enrolment link
//
// "A LINK OR QR OPENS THE ENROLMENT PAGE ON THE DEVICE", and this is the step that page takes once
// the person has read what the company will and will not see, and consented. It starts one
// enrolment, of the link's ownership kind, held by the person who opened it.
//
// THE LINK IS THE GRANT (the spec lane, 22 October 2026, ONPLO-3007). Opening one asks for no
// permission: the link's secret part, and its one-time code when it asks for one, are the proof,
// and the link's own "who may use it" decides who may open it. Minting the link was the
// Administrator act; the person who opens it completes it with their consent and their passkey.
//
// WHO MAY USE IT. `members` — a member of this account environment. `anyone` — anyone signed in to
// it, members and guests alike. `team` — somebody in the link's team, and anybody else is refused
// `enrolment_link_for_team`. And whoever may use it, "Your own device is member-only": a guest opening a link that fixes it is
// refused with the reason (decision 0526).
//
// THE LINK IS LOOKED FOR IN THE ACCOUNT ENVIRONMENT THIS CREDENTIAL ACTS IN, AND NOWHERE ELSE.
// Somebody with no place in the company that handed it out reads `enrolment_link_not_found`, whose
// `detail` says to ask that company to invite them. It is the same answer as a secret part that
// was never made, so a caller learns nothing about another account environment from it.
//
// A LINK THAT TAKES NO MORE DEVICES SAYS WHY: `enrolment_link_expired`, `enrolment_link_used_up`
// or `enrolment_link_stopped`, and `detail` says to ask whoever handed it out for a new one ("the
// person who opens a dead link reads why and who to ask"). A link whose Links & codes door was shut
// after it was made is refused `enrolment_door_shut`.
//
// THE DEVICE'S KIND IS SAID HERE, and one the link does not allow is refused
// `device_kind_not_allowed`. A computer is finished by the desktop app, with
// `completeEnrolmentThroughLink`. A phone or tablet only starts here: "the browser hands over to
// the operating system's own management prompt", and the operating system finishes it at its own
// door, which is not declared yet.
//
// THE USE IS COUNTED WHEN THE ENROLMENT FINISHES, never here, so an enrolment nobody finishes
// spends nothing. Each one finished through the link adds one to its `use_count`.
//
// IT ASKS YOU TO PROVE IT IS YOU: "The person consents and signs in with their passkey before
// anything is installed." Refused `passkey_proof_required` until you do, as `startEnrolment` is.
//
// AND IT SAYS WHICH PRIVACY NOTICE THE PERSON CONSENTED TO: "Opening it on the device shows the
// privacy notice for that kind and asks for consent". `privacy_notice_version` is the version of
// the link's ownership kind the page showed, and the enrolment keeps it. One that is not the latest
// is refused `privacy_notice_not_the_latest`, and `detail` says to read it again, so the page shows
// the notice again.
//
// AN ENROLMENT NOBODY FINISHES IS CLEARED AFTER SEVEN DAYS, as every enrolment is.
//
// Takes any type of body and a specified content type, and returns a wrapper object for the known response body format(s).
//
// Corresponds with POST /enrolment-link-enrolments (the `StartEnrolmentThroughLink` operationId).
func (c *ClientWithResponses) StartEnrolmentThroughLinkWithBodyWithResponse(ctx context.Context, contentType string, body io.Reader, reqEditors ...RequestEditorFn) (*StartEnrolmentThroughLinkResponse, error) {
	rsp, err := c.StartEnrolmentThroughLinkWithBody(ctx, contentType, body, reqEditors...)
	if err != nil {
		return nil, err
	}
	return ParseStartEnrolmentThroughLinkResponse(rsp)
}

