// CompleteEnrolmentThroughLinkWithBodyWithResponse Finish enrolling your computer through an enrolment link
//
// THE SECOND HALF OF AN ENROLMENT STARTED THROUGH A LINK, ON A COMPUTER: the desktop app finishes
// it in the person's own session, as `completeEnrolment` finishes this computer's. The request and
// the answer are that operation's, and so is the order: identity is told the device exists, then
// asked for its certificate, and only then is the device's record written. A try identity could
// not be reached for is finished by sending it again.
//
// IT ASKS FOR NO PERMISSION, as starting it did: the link was the grant. ONLY WHOEVER STARTED IT
// MAY FINISH IT, and to anybody else it does not exist.
//
// THE LINK IS READ AGAIN, AND ITS USE COUNTED. A link that took its last device, expired or was
// stopped since this enrolment started finishes nothing (`enrolment_link_used_up`,
// `enrolment_link_expired`, `enrolment_link_stopped`), and neither does one whose door was shut
// (`enrolment_door_shut`). One that is still open counts this device, in the same step that writes
// it, so a link never enrols more devices than its `max_use_count`.
//
// A COMPUTER, AND NOTHING ELSE. An enrolment started for a phone or tablet is finished by the
// operating system at its own door, and is refused here `enrolment_door_mismatch`, as is a platform
// that is not a computer's. One started any other way than through a link is finished by
// `completeEnrolment`, and is refused here the same way.
//
// WHERE THE DEVICE LANDS. In the link's group, following the link's setup, and in the Links & codes
// door's for each one the link leaves out. Identity is told the device joined the group after the
// certificate, and the device follows the setup by itself, at its latest version, enforced. A setup
// that does not fit a computer is not applied, and the device follows what it would.
//
// Takes any type of body and a specified content type, and returns a wrapper object for the known response body format(s).
//
// Corresponds with POST /enrolment-link-enrolments/{enrolment_id}/completion (the `CompleteEnrolmentThroughLink` operationId).
