// setup.
//
// THE ANSWER CARRIES THE LINK'S SECRET PART, AND ITS ONE-TIME CODE WHEN IT ASKS FOR ONE, ONCE. The
// secret part is what the link or QR carries; whoever holds it may start an enrolment through the
// link while it is open. The one-time code is "a short code shown to them separately, so a
// forwarded link alone enrols nothing". Neither is kept, only a hash of each, and neither is shown
// again: to show a QR again, make a new link.
//
// THE LINKS & CODES DOOR MUST BE OPEN, and a shut one refuses it (`enrolment_door_shut`): a link
// through a shut door would enrol nothing. The door ships shut.
//
// A COMPUTER, OR A PHONE OR TABLET. A server, a Chromebook, a screen and a one-job thing each have
// a door of their own (the spec lane, 21 October 2026).
//
// WHO MAY USE IT WIDENS WHO MAY OPEN THE LINK, NEVER WHICH OWNERSHIP KIND IT FIXES: "Your own
// device is member-only, and a guest who opens such a link is refused with the reason." That
// refusal, and the check of members or a team, are the enrolment's (`startEnrolmentThroughLink`).
//
// WHO MAY MAKE ONE IS WHO MAY USE THE LINKS & CODES DOOR, and anybody else is refused
// `enrolment_door_not_for_you`.
//
// THE GROUP AND THE SETUP follow the doors' rules: "It starts from the door's default and may be
// narrowed per link." `null` is the Links & codes door's own. A group you may not see answers as
// one that is not there, and a setup kept to its maker is refused (`setup_is_its_makers_own`).
//
// MAILED TO ONE PERSON, WHEN `mail_to` NAMES THEM (ONPLO-2951). The address is kept for that one send and
// never shown afterwards: the link says `mailed`, and its event says the same, never to whom. The mail
// carries the link, when it ends and the company's name, and never the one-time code, so a forwarded
// mail alone enrols nothing where the link asks for one. `mailed` says it was asked for, not that it
// arrived. A server not yet handed what a mail needs answers 501, and nothing is made.
//
