// ListLifecycleUpcomingWithResponse What is coming up in your devices' lives, earliest first
//
// LIFECYCLE'S UPCOMING TAB: "warranties ending, leases ending, reclaims due, repairs open and
// exemptions ending, worst first". One row per device and thing coming up: a device with both a
// warranty and a lease ending has two.
//
// WORST FIRST IS BY DATE, EARLIEST FIRST, so anything already past comes first (the spec lane,
// 2 November 2026, on ONPLO-3852). Rows on one day go in the page's order: warranty, lease,
// reclaim, repair, exemption. Then by device id, so a page never moves under a cursor.
//
// EACH KIND'S DAY:
//
//	warranty_ending    the warranty's end
//	lease_ending       the lease's end
//	reclaim_due        the day the member left, by UTC, plus how long the reclaim may go
//	                   unanswered, the day it escalates: 14 days, or one when nobody removed the
//	                   member (ONPLO-3850, ONPLO-3238). The company's own setting is not read yet
//	                   (ONPLO-2162)
//	repair_open        the day it was sent, in the zone it was sent in: it has no date of its own
//	exemption_ending   the day its end moment falls on, in the zone it names (decision 0661)
//
// WHICH ROWS. A warranty, a lease or an exemption is listed from the day the Alert lead time
// reaches it, 60 days ahead, by UTC: the page's default, since the company's own number is not
// read yet (ONPLO-2162). A warranty or a lease already ended stays until its date is changed or
// the device is retired. A reclaim and a repair are listed while they are open. A device two
// leavers held in turn lists the latest leaving's reclaim, as `Device.reclaim` answers. A retired
// or recycled device lists nothing.
//
// AN EXEMPTION IS COMPLIANCE'S, READ AND NEVER KEPT. Compliance answers only one still standing,
// so one that has run out leaves the list by itself. It cannot be asked for "those ending", only
// about devices, so every device you may see is asked about, a hundred at a time: the cost of
// this read grows with the fleet, as `countDevices`' does. Compliance being away answers 503
// `compliance_unavailable`, never a list missing its exemptions.
//
// EACH DEVICE IS ASKED ABOUT, AS ON THE LIST. Each row is judged by `devices:device.read`:
// somebody given one laptop is answered that laptop's rows.
//
// A PAGE ANSWERED IS A LOOK (decision 0675): one event that names no device.
//
// Returns a wrapper object for the known response body format(s).
//
// Corresponds with GET /lifecycle-upcoming (the `ListLifecycleUpcoming` operationId).
