// DeleteSoftwareItemWithResponse Remove a software item
//
// "REMOVING AN ASSIGNMENT OFFERS 'uninstall' OR 'leave installed' rather than deciding for you."
// `on_removal` says which; left out, the item's own `on_removal` holds. A Blocked item installed
// nothing, so for one it is not read.
//
// A PACKAGE'S VERSION IS LET GO ONCE THE ITEM IS GONE: Devices' use is taken off it, and the
// version stays named and kept in Storage (decision 0833 rule 3). The item is removed first, so
// the file is never left unprotected while an item still names it. When Storage cannot be asked
// right then, the item is still removed, and Devices records the use it still owes Storage to
// take off; a worker of Devices' asks Storage again on every pass until Storage takes it off
// (ONPLO-2923).
//
// ONE AUDIT EVENT, naming what was chosen.
//
