// UpdateSoftwareItemWithBodyWithResponse Change a software item
//
// "EDIT AN ITEM — its source, its version policy, its install command and detection rule, and
// whether it is required or there to install." Only what is sent changes.
//
// NEVER MAKES AN ITEM REQUIRED. Making one Required asks for the push permission as well
// (decision 0721 rule 1), so it is `makeSoftwareItemRequired`; `mode` here is available to
// install or Blocked. TAKING A REQUIRED ITEM BACK to available to install stays here: it installs
// nothing.
//
// WHAT A REQUIRED ITEM INSTALLS IS NOT CHANGED HERE. A new source or version policy on a Required
// item puts different software on every device it applies to at their next check-in, which is
// pushing, so it also asks for the push permission (decision 0721 rule 1, as the spec lane reads
// it): that is `changeRequiredSoftwareItemInstallation`, and sending either for a Required item
// here is refused (`required_item_has_its_own_operation`). Its name and what happens on removal change here.
//
// A BLOCKED ITEM HAS NO SOURCE. Changing an item to Blocked sends `blocked_software` and
// `source: null`; changing one from Blocked sends a source. Anything else is
// `unprocessable_request`.
//
// MOVING AN ITEM ONTO AN APP FROM A CONNECTED STORE IS `moveSoftwareItemToConnectedStore`: it
// points the item at a connection, which also asks `integrations:connection.assign`, so such a
// source sent here is refused (`connected_store_item_has_its_own_operation`). Moving an item OFF
// one is here: it points at nothing new, and Devices takes its use of the connection back.
//
// Takes any type of body and a specified content type, and returns a wrapper object for the known response body format(s).
//
// Corresponds with PATCH /software-items/{software_item_id} (the `UpdateSoftwareItem` operationId).
func (c *ClientWithResponses) UpdateSoftwareItemWithBodyWithResponse(ctx context.Context, softwareItemId SoftwareItemId, contentType string, body io.Reader, reqEditors ...RequestEditorFn) (*UpdateSoftwareItemResponse, error) {
	rsp, err := c.UpdateSoftwareItemWithBody(ctx, softwareItemId, contentType, body, reqEditors...)
	if err != nil {
		return nil, err
	}
	return ParseUpdateSoftwareItemResponse(rsp)
}

