// TrySoftwareInstallAgainOnDevicesWithBodyWithResponse Try a failed install once more on a selection of devices
//
// TRY AGAIN "ON THE WHOLE SELECTION" of an item's Failed list (Personal environment → Devices
// app → App → Software, ONPLO-3665): `trySoftwareInstallAgain` on each device named, asked once.
// Each install that moves goes back to waiting, and the device is handed the item again at its
// next check-in.
//
// A SELECTION IS UP TO 200 DEVICES BY ID, each named once.
//
// "EACH ONE ASKS ONCE, NAMES HOW MANY DEVICES IT WILL TOUCH" (Business environment → Devices
// app → Company devices). The devices it moves are those named that you may act on, that are in
// this account environment, that are not retired, and whose install failed for the version the
// item installs now. Until `expected_device_count` says exactly that number, the call is refused
// `device_count_to_confirm`, `detail` says the number, and nothing is written. When none would
// move, nothing is asked and the answer records nothing.
//
// EVERY DEVICE NAMED IS ANSWERED, NEVER SKIPPED. One that moved is in `installs`, as it now
// stands. Every other is in `not_tried_again` with why: `device_not_found` for one you may not
// act on, alike with one that does not exist or is another environment's; `device_is_retired`;
// and `install_not_failed` for an install that worked, one still waiting, an item the device was
// never handed, and one that failed for an older version, which is waiting for the new one
// already.
//
// EACH DEVICE IS ASKED ITS OWN PERMISSION, AND NOTHING ACROSS THE ACCOUNT ENVIRONMENT, as for
// one device: "given on one device or on all of them". Holding it on a device, or on a group the
// device is in, is enough for that device.
//
// AN ITEM THAT IS NOT THERE ANSWERS 404, the same for one in another environment, and nothing is
// written.
//
// ONE AUDIT RECORD PER DEVICE MOVED, naming who asked, as for one device. Either all of them are
// recorded or none is. No bulk action's job is recorded: trying an install again records no
// action on the device, and a job counts actions.
//
// Takes any type of body and a specified content type, and returns a wrapper object for the known response body format(s).
//
// Corresponds with POST /software-items/{software_item_id}/another-tries (the `TrySoftwareInstallAgainOnDevices` operationId).
func (c *ClientWithResponses) TrySoftwareInstallAgainOnDevicesWithBodyWithResponse(ctx context.Context, softwareItemId SoftwareItemId, contentType string, body io.Reader, reqEditors ...RequestEditorFn) (*TrySoftwareInstallAgainOnDevicesResponse, error) {
	rsp, err := c.TrySoftwareInstallAgainOnDevicesWithBody(ctx, softwareItemId, contentType, body, reqEditors...)
	if err != nil {
		return nil, err
	}
	return ParseTrySoftwareInstallAgainOnDevicesResponse(rsp)
}

// TrySoftwareInstallAgainOnDevicesWithResponse Try a failed install once more on a selection of devices
//
// TRY AGAIN "ON THE WHOLE SELECTION" of an item's Failed list (Personal environment → Devices
// app → App → Software, ONPLO-3665): `trySoftwareInstallAgain` on each device named, asked once.
// Each install that moves goes back to waiting, and the device is handed the item again at its
// next check-in.
//
// A SELECTION IS UP TO 200 DEVICES BY ID, each named once.
//
// "EACH ONE ASKS ONCE, NAMES HOW MANY DEVICES IT WILL TOUCH" (Business environment → Devices
// app → Company devices). The devices it moves are those named that you may act on, that are in
// this account environment, that are not retired, and whose install failed for the version the
// item installs now. Until `expected_device_count` says exactly that number, the call is refused
// `device_count_to_confirm`, `detail` says the number, and nothing is written. When none would
// move, nothing is asked and the answer records nothing.
//
// EVERY DEVICE NAMED IS ANSWERED, NEVER SKIPPED. One that moved is in `installs`, as it now
// stands. Every other is in `not_tried_again` with why: `device_not_found` for one you may not
// act on, alike with one that does not exist or is another environment's; `device_is_retired`;
// and `install_not_failed` for an install that worked, one still waiting, an item the device was
// never handed, and one that failed for an older version, which is waiting for the new one
// already.
//
// EACH DEVICE IS ASKED ITS OWN PERMISSION, AND NOTHING ACROSS THE ACCOUNT ENVIRONMENT, as for
// one device: "given on one device or on all of them". Holding it on a device, or on a group the
// device is in, is enough for that device.
//
// AN ITEM THAT IS NOT THERE ANSWERS 404, the same for one in another environment, and nothing is
// written.
//
// ONE AUDIT RECORD PER DEVICE MOVED, naming who asked, as for one device. Either all of them are
// recorded or none is. No bulk action's job is recorded: trying an install again records no
// action on the device, and a job counts actions.
//
// Takes a body of the `application/json` content type, and returns a wrapper object for the known response body format(s).
//
// Corresponds with POST /software-items/{software_item_id}/another-tries (the `TrySoftwareInstallAgainOnDevices` operationId).
