// A NEW SOURCE OR VERSION POLICY ON A REQUIRED ITEM IS PUSHING. "A Required item installs by itself
// at the next check-in", so a different package, a different pinned or minimum version, or a
// different install command or detection rule (both are part of a package's source) puts
// different software on every device it applies to. It asks for `devices:software-item.deploy`
// beside changing the item, every time (decision 0721 rule 1, as the spec lane reads it on
// 2026-10-17). Only what is sent changes.
//
// ONLY FOR A REQUIRED ITEM (`software_item_is_not_required`); any other changes its source and
// version policy through `updateSoftwareItem`, because nothing installs until a person taps. A
// FLOW OR AN AGENT NEVER GETS HERE, for the reason `createRequiredSoftwareItem` gives.
//
// NEVER ONTO AN APP FROM A CONNECTED STORE. That would ask a third permission, pointing the item
// at a connection, and an operation asks at most one beside its own (decision 0657). Take the
// item off Required with `updateSoftwareItem`, move it with `moveSoftwareItemToConnectedStore`,
// and make it Required again (`connected_store_item_has_its_own_operation`).
//
// Takes a body of the `application/json` content type, and returns a wrapper object for the known response body format(s).
//
// Corresponds with PATCH /software-items/{software_item_id}/required-installation (the `ChangeRequiredSoftwareItemInstallation` operationId).
