// CreateUpdateScheduleWithBodyWithResponse Add an update schedule
//
// A SCHEDULE OF YOUR OWN, beside the three that ship: "+ New schedule".
//
// IT NAMES AT LEAST ONE GROUP. A schedule is "a rule over groups", and only Everyone holds
// none. A GROUP FOLLOWS ONE SCHEDULE AT A TIME: naming a group that follows another schedule
// moves it here, and the schedule it left no longer lists it. Read `listUpdateSchedules`
// first to tell a person which groups will move.
//
// SPEED DECIDES THE DAYS. With `fast`, `standard` or `careful` the deferral and the deadline
// follow the word and are not sent. With `custom` both are sent. Sending days beside another
// speed, or `custom` without them, is refused as `unprocessable_request`.
//
// A GROUP IS ASKED ABOUT ONE BY ONE. Seeing a group can be given on one group alone, so the
// door asks which of the groups named you may see (`devices:group.read`, decision 0752), and
// one you may not see answers exactly as one that does not exist.
//
// Takes any type of body and a specified content type, and returns a wrapper object for the known response body format(s).
//
// Corresponds with POST /update-schedules (the `CreateUpdateSchedule` operationId).
